{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKoWE79ncxPmYa1vUzF7qU","type":"tool_result","content":"15:to evaluations of the multilinear extensions `p̂` and `q̂` at a random point. The GKR protocol applies to the fractional summation tree (segment tree) built from the `2^n` leaf fractions `(p(x), q(x))`.\n105:In the natural (big-endian) ordering, leaf at index `i` corresponds to hypercube point `(x_1, ..., x_n)` with `i = x_1 * 2^{n-1} + ... + x_n * 2^0`. In a standard segment tree, the children of node `i` are at positions `2i` and `2i+1` — adjacent elements — so each layer pairs neighbors at stride 1.\n[rerun: b10]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AtdyzMWMsZyBSR8LM8TksV","session_id":"5bb7d674-211a-472f-a536-7708d797558d","uuid":"0bffa0f9-52e6-4001-b449-311e460c84e5","timestamp":"2026-04-15T02:31:02.631Z"}
