{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qK3rZ2BfJTgiEvkAzzuJ3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a very clear picture. Let me create a final comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Complete Trace Commit Code Path Analysis\n\nI've traced the entire code flow for the Trace Commit operation in the CUDA-accelerated STARK prover. Here's the comprehensive breakdown:\n\n### 1. **High-Level Flow: How Segments Are Grouped**\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/hal.rs` (lines 161-184)\n- **Input**: Each AIR segment has:\n  - `preprocessed_data` (optional) - single committed preprocessing trace\n  - `cached_mains` (Vec) - multiple committed main trace segments\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (lines 187-271, 304-317)\n- Function: `prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu()`\n- Creates one **StackedPcsData2** per segment (not per AIR):\n  - `common_main_stacked` (1 per prover)\n  - For each AIR: 1 per preprocessed_data + 1 per cached_mains entry\n  - Each gets its own `stacked_commit()` call\n- All StackedPcsData2 instances collected into `stacked_per_commit: Vec<StackedPcsData2<D>>`\n\n### 2. **Exact Call Chain: stacked_commit() Function**\n\n#### **Entry Point (GPU Backend)**\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs` (lines 61-73)\n```rust\nimpl TraceCommitter<GenericGpuBackend<HS>> for GpuDevice {\n    fn commit(&self, traces: &[&DeviceMatrix<F>]) -> Result<...> {\n        stacked_commit::<HS::MerkleHash>(\n            l_skip, n_stack, log_blowup, k_whir,\n            traces,\n            prover_config\n        )\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### **stacked_commit() Main Implementation**\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` (lines 48-84)\n\n```\nstacked_commit::<MH>()  [MH = hash scheme]\n├─ get_stacked_layout(l_skip, n_stack, traces)\n│  └─ Groups trace