{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XpU2umr5aRDTc2ECZFFHta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UXxiMKmEbBGPwYYg21YMSP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-0430-multistream-mle-round-eval\n\nOverlap the logup and zerocheck evaluation paths within each MLE sumcheck round using OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Currently `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` runs logup monomial/batch_mle evaluation and zerocheck monomial/batch_mle/par-Y evaluation sequentially on the default CUDA stream. These paths are independent (separate input combination data, separate output arrays) and can execute concurrently on different CUDA streams, following the same multi-stream pattern used successfully for Round 0 (3.28x) and GKR input eval (1.67x). At APC 300, individual MLE kernels are small (10-500µs) and don't saturate the GPU, leaving SM capacity for concurrent execution from a second stream.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":166999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bb7d674-211a-472f-a536-7708d797558d","uuid":"5d0ea1f7-6575-4288-8308-548afb427687"}
