while keeping all the immutable data accessible to both threads. I'm thinking through when multi-streaming becomes worthwhile based on trace saturation. At APC 0 with mostly large traces saturating the GPU, single-streaming is fine since there's no spare capacity anyway. But at APC 300 with many smaller traces, there's room to run multiple kernels concurrently, so multi-streaming would actually help. I should add a threshold—only enable multi-streaming when there are enough early eval traces to justify it, like 100 or more per round, which keeps APC 0 running efficiently while unlocking parallelism at APC 300.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2265,"cache_read_input_tokens":168451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2265},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bb7d674-211a-472f-a536-7708d797558d","uuid":"e464cc66-01df-49af-bcc5-112262e551dd"}
