spawned closures to `to_host_on_current_stream()`, and pre-allocate the intermediates buffers for both paths before spawning threads. This eliminates both the COPY_EVENT mutex and most MEMORY_MANAGER mutex contention. The pre-allocation approach would mirror the GKR input eval pattern that successfully pre-allocated buffers per thread.\n\n### B. Consider a simpler two-kernel overlap approach\n\nInstead of splitting all six evaluation steps across two threads, consider overlapping only the dominant cost pairs. If the logup monomial batch (a single kernel launch + D2H) and the zerocheck monomial par-Y batch (a single kernel launch + D2H) are the two heaviest operations, overlapping just these two with a minimal thread scope would reduce complexity. The late eval traces (num_y=1) are negligible in cost and could remain sequential.\n\n### C. Measure per-step kernel times first\n\nBefore implementing, instrument the six evaluation steps with `std::time::Instant` or NVTX ranges to get per-step wall-clock times. If one path dominates (e.g., logup batched takes 4ms and zerocheck takes 1ms), the overlap gains are capped at 1ms per round, making the optimization not worthwhile. This measurement is cheap and would either confirm or reject the plan's viability.\n\n## Assessment\n\nThere are two design-level blockers: the `COPY_EVENT` mutex serialization (finding 1) and the `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex contention (finding 2). Without addressing both, the multi-stream approach will not achieve meaningful parallelism -- the threads will alternate between holding one mutex or the other, effectively executing sequentially with added thread spawn overhead. This is the same failure mode documented in the `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0` log entry.\n\nThe plan is not prototype-ready as written. To become implementable:\n1. All `to_host()` calls in the spawned closures must be replaced with `to_host_on_current_stream()`.\n2. Intermediates buffers for both paths must be pre-allocated before spawning threads to minimize MEMORY_MANAGER mutex contention.\n3. The explicit `current_stream_sync()` location must be specified.\n4. All `self` field borrows must be extracted before the scope block.\n\nThe strongest part of the plan is the correct identification that the logup and zerocheck evaluation paths are mathematically independent and write to non-overlapping output arrays. The data dependency analysis (finding that `logup_out`/`logup_tilde_evals` vs `zc_out`/`zerocheck_tilde_evals` are disjoint) is accurate based on the code.\n\nEven with the blockers fixed, the expected benefit is marginal. MLE Rounds is 178ms at APC 300 (3.1% of total proof time), the log shows kernel execution dominates, and the per-round overlap window is small. A realistic estimate with fixes applied is 10-20ms, not 20-40ms. Whether this justifies the added complexity (Send wrappers, borrow splitting, threshold tuning, two stream-sync changes) is questionable."}],"totalDurationMs":175953,"totalTokens":77297,"totalToolUseCount":41,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":73096,"output_tokens":2627,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1573},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2627,"cache_read_input_tokens":73096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":23,"searchCount":16,"bashCount":2,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014dLrXn8nqVe7qXYqtbYJY7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The reviewer found two design-level blockers:\n\n1. **COPY_EVENT mutex serialization**: All `to_host()` calls acquire a global mutex. Both threads would contend on this, effectively serializing the D2H copies. Fix: use `to_host_on_current_stream()` instead.\n\n2. **MEMORY_MANAGER mutex contention**: The global memory manager mutex serializes all GPU allocations. Both threads would contend on this, similar to the failed `multistream-stacked-reduction-round0` task. Fix: pre-allocate intermediates buffers before spawning threads.\n\nAdditional findings:\n3. Interpolation sync point location not precisely specified\n\n\n4. The savings estimate is too optimistic — realistically 10-20ms with fixes, not 20-40ms\n5. Self borrow splitting is incomplete\n6. The threshold choice lacks justification\n\nThe reviewer's verdict is that while the core independence analysis holds up, the implementation isn't prototype-ready yet. Even with all the fixes, the expected benefit of 10-20ms is marginal and might not be worth the added complexity. The MEMORY_MANAGER mutex issue is particularly concerning since it's what derailed the stacked-reduction attempt before. I need to weigh whether to push forward with these fixes or reconsider the whole approach.\n\nActually, the reviewer also flagged that `to_host_on_current_stream` already exists for exactly this multi-stream scenario, and the pre-allocation pattern has proven reliable in past work. So I can address the blockers: switch to `to_host_on_current_stream()` in the spawned closures, pre-allocate all intermediate buffers upfront, pin down the exact `current_stream_sync()` call, flesh out the complete borrow splitting, and revise the savings down to 10-20ms. Even though that's marginal, it's still above the 10ms threshold that's been acceptable before, and it does improve the APC 300/APC 0 scaling ratio by reducing inverse-scaling effects.\n\nNow I need to finalize the revised plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3342,"cache_read_input_tokens":175755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3342},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bb7d674-211a-472f-a536-7708d797558d","uuid":"4c5217b9-102b-4b83-8c12-0e2de9c52e66"}
