{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TgdAwasYbhMW2qSfkJcajJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-0430-multistream-mle-round-eval\n2\t\n3\tOverlap the logup and zerocheck evaluation paths within each MLE sumcheck round using OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Currently `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` runs logup monomial/batch_mle evaluation and zerocheck monomial/batch_mle/par-Y evaluation sequentially on the default CUDA stream. These paths are independent (separate input combination data, separate output arrays) and can execute concurrently on different CUDA streams, following the same multi-stream pattern used successfully for Round 0 (3.28x) and GKR input eval (1.67x). At APC 300, individual MLE kernels are small (10-500µs) and don't saturate the GPU, leaving SM capacity for concurrent execution from a second stream.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bb7d674-211a-472f-a536-7708d797558d","uuid":"55c40f24-f80e-4c14-9be7-7fc467f96339","timestamp":"2026-04-15T03:02:25.153Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-0430-multistream-mle-round-eval\n\nOverlap the logup and zerocheck evaluation paths within each MLE sumcheck round using OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams. Currently `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` runs logup monomial/batch_mle evaluation and zerocheck monomial/batch_mle/par-Y evaluation sequentially on the default CUDA stream. These paths are independent (separate input combination data, separate output arrays) and can execute concurrently on different CUDA streams, following the same multi-stream pattern used successfully for Round 0 (3.28x) and GKR input eval (1.67x). At APC 300, individual MLE kernels are small (10-500µs) and don't saturate the GPU, leaving SM capacity for concurrent execution from a second stream.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
